      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`server_arguments_undocumented.txt` is the ratchet list of live `ServerArgs` flags that have no row in `server_arguments.mdx`. Its header says it \"may only shrink\". Four PD-disaggregation flags on it are user-facing knobs that people running PD deployments look for, but none of them is in the docs today:\n\n- `--disaggregation-enable-kv-checksum`\n- `--disaggregation-decode-retraction-backup`\n- `--disaggregation-decode-extra-slots`\n- `--disaggregation-decode-host-receive-threshold`\n\n## Modifications\n\n- I added a row for each flag next to the related flags already in the PD section (transfer backend, offload-kvcache, num-reserved-decode-tokens, polling interval).\n- Descriptions, defaults and choices come straight from each field's `Arg(help=...)`, default value and `choices` in `python/sglang/srt/arg_groups/fields/disagg.py`, so the docs match the CLI. I didn't change any wording.\n- I removed the four flags from `server_arguments_undocumented.txt`.\n\nDocs only. No code changes.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nI searched open PRs for `server_arguments_undocumented`, each flag name, and \"backfill server arguments\". None adds rows for these flags.\n\n## Tests\n\n```text\n$ python -m pytest test/registered/unit/server_args/test_server_args_docs_coverage.py -q\n4 passed\n\n# with the allowlist removal but without the new rows (sanity check that the test guards this):\nFAILED ...::test_no_new_undocumented_flags\n1 failed, 3 passed\n```\n\nThe tests ran on CPU. Every row has 4 cells, and every flag named in the doc still registers.\n\nAI assistance was used; I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40611658194](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40611658194)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40611658139](https://github.com/sg